# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the card telemetry window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of
# tp4/fusion-1 (or the integrated head) and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The job is a
# template only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the minutes, the stop rules and how to read the telemetry.
# ONE IMAGE: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag the integrated pack's B0 builds from the pushed head (sed -i 's/tp4-fusion-1/<tag>/' *.env). The sidecar is not in the image:
# it runs on the host from the checkout (scripts/ci/card_telemetry.sh), so a commit that only changes it needs no new image. The cards are under development: this job never stops, starts or hands back
# the node agent.
# TEL1 (TIMED, card telemetry): the SOLO prefill ladder (PL1's prefill_ladder_solo) on the production profile, UNPROFILED, with C2_TELEMETRY=1. prefill_ladder_solo: four real-code prompts of about
# 4,096 / 32,768 / 131,072 / 253,920 tokens, ONE request at a time with nothing else running, a 16-token answer: the time to first token and the prefill rate of each rung. The sidecar reads every
# chip's ARC telemetry once a second for the whole step (boot and warm-up included) and prints one line per chip at the end: AICLK under load (min/median against fmax), maximum power (chip and
# board), maximum temperature (ASIC and GDDR) and whether any throttler engaged and which. WHY: the prefill op profile against its unprofiled twin showed a uniform ~13% device-side slowdown in the
# sustained run that scales with SDPA time, which AICLK or power/current throttling would explain (13% of 1350 MHz is about 1175 MHz); the profiled run idles ~2.8 s every 16 layers, the sustained one does not.
# READ: (1) the `[TELEMETRY]` lines of the step log (also telemetry-smoke/telemetry-summary.txt and .json in the results; the per-second rows are telemetry-smoke/telemetry.csv.gz) and the decode check
# in the first one (`decode check ok`: the raw table agrees with pyluwen's own decode of the static tags; MISMATCH or UNAVAILABLE means read nothing from the rest); (2) per chip, over the
# solo rungs (the CSV `ts` is unix time: the ladder rows' started_at / first_at in the smoke results bound each rung): loaded AICLK median at or near fmax and `throttler: none engaged` REFUTES
# clock throttling (look at DRAM, NOC and dispatch next); a loaded AICLK median about 12% or more under fmax with a named limiter (tdp, fast_tdc, tdc, thm, board_power, gddr_thm, doppler_*) is the
# explanation, and the limiter says which of the power, current or thermal limits to attack; `kernel NOPs started` means the firmware slowed the kernels without lowering AICLK; (3) the
# rung times against the same ladder in the prefill pack's PL1 (the same prompts, no telemetry) to see that the sidecar did not move them. THE SIDECAR READS ONLY (AXI reads of the table the ARC
# firmware publishes, the read tt-smi makes; no ARC message, no write) and opens each chip for a moment per sample as the host's telemetry collector does. REQUIRES: the smoke test
# prefill_ladder_solo in the tagged commit (it is on tp4/prefill-1, not on tp4/fusion-1: merge that commit; the smoke client runs from the checkout, so no image rebuild is needed).
# TIMED: the ARC runner sets are at ZERO for this job; no build, no CI push, no other job beside it. Duration (estimate): boot 10 minutes, solo ladder 4 (about 98 s for the 254k rung), 25 minutes
# in all; the box is 40.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-traffic
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,prefill_ladder_solo
# Knowingly omits concurrent8_steady: without this key c2_serving_job.py refuses the job. The smoke check is unchanged, so the run still ends red on its eight-seat rule; read the logs.
C2_SMOKE_PARTIAL=card telemetry on the solo prefill ladder: its test list is fixed by the protocol, so concurrent8_steady is not run
C2_BOX_MINUTES=40
C2_TELEMETRY=1
